{"id":"n3-130","title":"必ずしも～とは限らない (kanarazushimo ～ towa kagiranai)","jlptLevel":3,"shortExplanation":"Not necessarily; not always.","longExplanation":"The 必ずしも～とは限らない grammar point is used to express that something is not necessarily or not always the case, indicating that a certain assumption may not hold true in all situations.","formation":"必ずしも + Statement + とは限らない","examples":[{"jp":"高いものが必ずしも良いとは限らない。","romaji":"Takai mono ga kanarazushimo yoi to wa kagiranai.","en":"Expensive things are not necessarily better.","words":[{"surface":"高い","vocabId":"1283190","reading":"たかい"},{"surface":"もの","vocabId":"1322990","reading":"もの"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"必ずしも","vocabId":"1487410","reading":"かならずしも"},{"surface":"良い","vocabId":"1605820","reading":"よい"},{"surface":"と","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"限ら","vocabId":"1264640","reading":"かぎる","baseForm":"限る"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[3,5,6,7,8]},{"jp":"有名な人が必ずしも幸せとは限らない。","romaji":"Yuumei na hito ga kanarazushimo shiawase to wa kagiranai.","en":"Famous people are not necessarily happy.","words":[{"surface":"有名","vocabId":"1541620","reading":"ゆうめい"},{"surface":"な","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"だ"},{"surface":"人","vocabId":"1580640","reading":"ひと"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"必ずしも","vocabId":"1487410","reading":"かならずしも"},{"surface":"幸せ","vocabId":"1594060","reading":"しあわせ"},{"surface":"と","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"限ら","vocabId":"1264640","reading":"かぎる","baseForm":"限る"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4,6,7,8,9]},{"jp":"外国語が話せる人が必ずしも英語が得意とは限らない。","romaji":"Gaikokugo ga hanaseru hito ga kanarazushimo eigo ga tokui to wa kagiranai.","en":"People who can speak a foreign language are not always good at English.","words":[{"surface":"外国","vocabId":"1203620","reading":"がいこく"},{"surface":"語","vocabId":"1270910","reading":"ご"},{"